From 74ce96fc247b7d4f62b7805d35c62b61e88bb42d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 07:10:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rust: sysfs: add root-device attribute groups

Add owned root-device and attribute-group abstractions for drivers
which expose control files directly below /sys/devices.

Allocate and pin the complete group and callback context before
publishing any attribute. Track the successfully created prefix and
remove it before callback state is cleared on registration unwind
and normal teardown.

Use an initialized-output Writer for show callbacks, handle empty store
buffers without constructing a slice from a possibly null pointer,
and cover writer accounting and partial-registration unwind with
KUnit tests.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
